    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.diff\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.11 (!at least latest Nightly build!)\n\n### Description\n\nWhen you start Neovim with an auto-session plugin that automatically loads session, mini.diff can trigger the LSP attach on all buffers loaded by auto-session. This may cause sluggish Neovim behavior and poor performance, depending on the project size.\n\nThe normal behavior is to attach only to visible windows/buffers on startup.\n\nHere is the stack trace from the nvim-lspconfig attach event that pointed me to mini.diff.\n\n```\n21:06:40 msg_show.lua_print stack traceback:\n  ...share/nvim/lazy/nvim-lspconfig/lua/lspconfig/configs.lua:82: in function <...share/nvim/lazy/nvim-lspconfig/lua/lspconfig/configs.lua:79>\n  [C]: in function 'nvim_exec_autocmds'\n  ...hare/nvim/lazy/lazy.nvim/lua/lazy/core/handler/event.lua:161: in function <...hare/nvim/lazy/lazy.nvim/lua/lazy/core/handler/event.lua:160>\n  [C]: in function 'xpcall'\n  .../.local/share/nvim/lazy/lazy.nvim/lua/lazy/core/util.lua:135: in function 'try'\n  ...hare/nvim/lazy/lazy.nvim/lua/lazy/core/handler/event.lua:160: in function 'trigger'\n  ...hare/nvim/lazy/lazy.nvim/lua/lazy/core/handler/event.lua:89: in function <...hare/nvim/lazy/lazy.nvim/lua/lazy/core/handler/event.lua:72>\n  [C]: in function 'nvim_cmd'\n  ...rew/Cellar/neovim/0.11.0/share/nvim/runtime/filetype.lua:36: in function <...rew/Cellar/neovim/0.11.0/share/nvim/runtime/filetype.lua:35>\n  [C]: in function 'pcall'\n  vim/shared.lua: in function <vim/shared.lua:0>\n  [C]: in function '_with'\n  ...rew/Cellar/neovim/0.11.0/share/nvim/runtime/filetype.lua:35: in function <...rew/Cellar/neovim/0.11.0/share/nvim/runtime/filetype.lua:10>\n  [C]: at 0x010489d194\n  [C]: in function 'pcall'\n  .../niba/.local/share/nvim/lazy/mini.diff/lua/mini/diff.lua:1800: in function 'buf_ensure_loaded'\n  .../niba/.local/share/nvim/lazy/mini.diff/lua/mini/diff.lua:464: in function 'enable'\n.../niba/.local/share/nvim/lazy/mini.diff/lua/mini/diff.lua:1037: in function ''\n```\n\n### Reproduction\n\nI use Lazy as my plugin manager. This issue is not easy to reproduce because you need:\n\n1.\tAn auto-session plugin that loads on startup.\n2.\tMini.diff with the \"VeryLazy\" event, which is the default setting on LazyVim.\n3.  Many buffers open in a large project or monorepo.\n\n\nWhat happens:\n\n1.\tYou start Neovim.\n2.\tThe auto-session plugin loads all buffers from the previous session.\n3.\tLazy calls mini.diff setup function which contains code that performs operations on all existing buffers.\n4.\tThis triggers the LSP attach event.\n\nThe workaround is to set ⁠`lazy=false` in the mini.diff configuration\n\n",
