        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\n\nYes, I can reproduce with 'mini.sessions'. The reason I haven't experienced it is because with using `later()` \"lazy-loading\" form 'mini.deps' the 'mini.diff' for me is set up when there only a single 'mini.starter' buffer.\n\nI am pretty there is an easy solution here. It fixes things for me, but I would like to ask you to see if it fixes your use case. Would you mind altering the '.../niba/.local/share/nvim/lazy/mini.diff/lua/mini/diff.lua' file on [this line](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/2e38ed16c2ced64bcd576986ccad4b18e2006e18/lua/mini/diff.lua#L1079) (actual line number seem to be a bit off in the traceback) to have `vim.api.nvim_buf_is_loaded` instead of `vim.api.nvim_buf_is_valid`. So it should be `  if not (vim.api.nvim_buf_is_loaded(buf) and vim.bo[buf].buftype == '' and vim.bo[buf].buflisted) then return end`. Does this solve the issue for you?",
